WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.493 --> 00:00:02.697
- Alright everybody, that
you so much for coming out.

00:00:02.697 --> 00:00:04.865
My name is Keith, and
I'm here from corporate

00:00:04.865 --> 00:00:07.771
to talk about our office
relationship policy.

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:10.490
- It was these two. They
were the ones making whoopee.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.216
- Oh yeah dude.

00:00:11.216 --> 00:00:13.170
- I just want to say
that I made a mistake,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.979
and I fully support the
ban on office romance.

00:00:15.979 --> 00:00:18.285
- Well, actually there is no ban.

00:00:18.285 --> 00:00:21.643
Believe it on not, yours
truly is in an office romance.

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:25.815
This is Kim, and we are in a fun,

00:00:25.815 --> 00:00:28.610
and professional, relationship.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.646
Isn't she the best? Look at that smile.

00:00:30.646 --> 00:00:32.383
I miss her so much. (laughs)

00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:33.555
I've been on the road for a week

00:00:33.555 --> 00:00:37.635
doing this presentation, but
I am flying home tonight.

00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:41.999
So Keith's Keys to a
successful office relationship.

00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:44.354
Number one is Respect.

00:00:46.054 --> 00:00:48.161
And respect not just for your co-lover,

00:00:49.536 --> 00:00:50.670
but for your co-worker as well.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.263
(coughing)

00:00:52.263 --> 00:00:55.162
Yup, it sounds like we
struck a chord there.

00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:56.822
Let's dive deeper into that, okay?

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:59.842
- Would that be deeper into
your relationship with...

00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:00.886
- Kim.

00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:02.268
- Kim! Right.

00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:04.328
- Great idea, let's use an example.

00:01:04.328 --> 00:01:07.650
So Kim's assistant, Jaime,
came to us a year ago

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.693
because he was feeling uncomfortable

00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:11.712
with setting up our dinner reservations.

00:01:11.712 --> 00:01:14.475
So we started handling it ourselves.

00:01:14.475 --> 00:01:15.636
- Oh no!

00:01:15.636 --> 00:01:18.027
- No no no, don't worry because we were,

00:01:18.027 --> 00:01:20.350
say it with me now, respectful.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.615
- [All] Respectful...

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:24.196
- And now Kim's professional
relationship with Jaime

00:01:24.196 --> 00:01:26.576
is stronger than ever, I promise you that.

00:01:26.576 --> 00:01:30.151
So, moving on to number
two of Keith's Keys.

00:01:32.503 --> 00:01:33.206
- Keith!

00:01:33.206 --> 00:01:34.750
- I know what you guys are gonna say,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.709
and it's an intentional typo.

00:01:38.921 --> 00:01:40.550
- Great typo Keith. Question?

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.235
- Yeah.

00:01:41.235 --> 00:01:43.294
- What role does communication have in,

00:01:43.294 --> 00:01:45.988
say, an office breakup?

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.148
- Well, I've never been part of

00:01:49.148 --> 00:01:51.714
a failed office relationship,
so I don't know.

00:01:51.714 --> 00:01:53.094
- Hypothetically.

00:01:53.094 --> 00:01:54.371
- Hypothetically.

00:01:56.479 --> 00:01:57.861
Well, I'd be devastated.

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:03.202
I would have trouble finding
light in this dark, dark world.

00:02:04.379 --> 00:02:07.840
But luckily, that will never happen to me.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.932
- Oh my god.

00:02:08.932 --> 00:02:10.352
- She's miraculous, isn't she?

00:02:10.352 --> 00:02:13.787
She is my everything, only second to

00:02:13.787 --> 00:02:17.433
Loafie, here. (laughs)

00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:19.577
(all groaning)

00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:20.259
- No!

00:02:20.259 --> 00:02:22.246
- Don't worry, I'm gonna
continue the presentation

00:02:22.246 --> 00:02:23.744
right after I get an eyeful of

00:02:23.744 --> 00:02:26.809
my best friend in the entire world.

00:02:26.809 --> 00:02:28.063
- Caylen, I still love you!

00:02:28.063 --> 00:02:28.830
- I knew it!

00:02:30.096 --> 00:02:31.384
- See?

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.984
Keith's Keys can lead to a
successful office relationship.

00:02:34.984 --> 00:02:37.582
- Great job, Keith! Mission accomplished.

00:02:37.582 --> 00:02:38.447
I'll see you out.

00:02:38.447 --> 00:02:40.757
- Actually, I have
dozens more Keith's Keys.

00:02:40.757 --> 00:02:43.184
- Well no need, because you were

00:02:43.184 --> 00:02:44.983
able to repair Caylen and Anna's

00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:47.421
disgusting mistake of a relationship.

00:02:47.421 --> 00:02:49.185
So let's give Keith a round of applause!

00:02:49.185 --> 00:02:53.361
- (applause) Yeah. Really good, yeah.

00:02:53.361 --> 00:02:54.274
- Thank you so much!

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:54.734
- Thank you!

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:55.395
(laughs)

00:02:55.395 --> 00:02:57.532
Oh, I'm blowing up! (laughs)

00:02:57.532 --> 00:02:58.477
(door slams)

00:03:01.048 --> 00:03:02.048
What?

00:03:03.668 --> 00:03:05.402
No! (screams in agony)

00:03:05.402 --> 00:03:07.000
- Do you think he knows? Or...

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.441
(lighthearted music)

00:03:10.441 --> 00:03:11.650
- Let's just wait it out.

00:03:13.177 --> 00:03:15.522
- We can move into my place.
- No.

00:03:15.522 --> 00:03:17.623
- It's a big van.
- No.

00:03:17.623 --> 00:03:18.784
(laughter)

